  { p: 'Who were the thralls?', op: ['Aristocrats', 'Slaves', 'Free men', 'Priests'], certa: 1, exp: 'Thralls were slaves, without rights; karls were free men.' },
  { p: 'Which king united England, Denmark and Norway in the North Sea Empire?', op: ['Cnut the Great', 'Harald Bluetooth', 'Alfred', 'William'], certa: 0, exp: 'Cnut reigned in England (1016), Denmark (1018) and Norway (1028).' },
  { p: 'In which battle did Harald Hardrada die in 1066?', op: ['Hastings', 'Clontarf', 'Stamford Bridge', 'Edington'], certa: 2, exp: 'On 25 September 1066, defeated by Harold Godwinson, three weeks before Hastings.' },
  { p: 'According to Arab sources, in which year did the Vikings attack Lisbon?', op: ['793', '844', '911', '1066'], certa: 1, exp: 'In 844 the fleet plundered Lisbon for about thirteen days and went on to Seville, but the sources (Ibn Idhari, Ibn Hayyan) are much later.' },
  { p: 'What did the DNA from grave Bj 581 at Birka reveal?', op: ['That it was a king', 'That it was a youth', 'That the skeleton was a woman’s', 'That it was a slave'], certa: 2, exp: 'The 2017 study identified a woman; some researchers debate whether she was a warrior.' }
